  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize emptying piles to turn over face-down cards. An empty pile is goldâ€”it lets you move any junk card there to unblock others. In 2/4 Suit, try to keep piles 'pure' (same suit) as much as possible so you can move them later.\n\nThe 'Tidy Up' Phase: Before dealing a new row, tidy up your runs. Make sure sequences are as consolidated as possible. If you have a choice between putting a 5-Hearts on a 6-Hearts or 6-Spades, choose Hearts.\n\nSacrificing a Run: Sometimes playing a 5-Hearts on a 6-Spades (blocking the run) is necessary to uncover a face-down card that might be a King. Uncovering cards > Maintaining runs.",
